# Models and artefacts
*.pkl
*.joblib
models/**
!models/.gitkeep
# The reference regressor IS a deliverable, not an artefact: the API loads it
# to produce a prediction and its TreeSHAP explanation, so a clone without it
# is a clone that cannot answer "why did you expect that reading". 2.3 MB per
# channel, and reproducible from the simulated network with one command.
!models/reference/
!models/reference/*.txt
!models/reference/report.json

# Old project â€” superseded, kept locally for reference only
SIH2026_Disaster_Engine_Master_Blueprint.pdf

# Raw ERA5 export -- committed for now so teammates can run without a handoff.
# It is the one file in the chain that CANNOT be regenerated.
.freebuff/

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# Dashboard build output â€” regenerate with `python -m dashboard.build`
dashboard/snapshot.json
# dashboard/wdqms.json is deliberately NOT ignored. It is 266 kB, it is the
# real IMD station list that the simulated network and every map are derived
# from, and rebuilding it needs a fetch from WMO. Keeping it out meant a fresh
# clone could not build the site at all -- and a deploy host that cannot reach
# WMO still could not. It is small and it is the seed of everything.
# generated by `python -m simulate.faults_and_export`
dashboard/sim_map.json
dashboard/console.html

# Basemap tile cache — regenerable, sometimes large
data/tilecache/
data/uscrn_tx/

# ---- generated, and it was all committed once ----
#
# Every path here is produced by a script in this repository from something
# else in this repository. Committing them meant the same bytes existed twice
# under two names, and the copy in git went stale the moment the generator ran.

# scripts/export_static.py -- 6.7 MB duplicating dashboard/ for static hosting
web/public/api/

# ppt_build/render.py renders these from the .pptx
ppt_build/render/

# The ingest store. Generated at runtime; the readings in it are a record of
# this machine, not of the project.
data/skyguard.db*

# PlatformIO build output: toolchain artefacts, ~1 MB binaries, regenerated
# by `pio run`. Never source.
.pio/
